+
+# PLAN-012: Playback speed control on the Review page player
+
+## Status
+
+draft
+
+## Context
+
+The Review page renders `SessionAudioPlayer`
+(`web/src/components/audio-player.tsx`), a custom transport over a hidden
+`<audio>` element, synced to transcript cues via `onTimeUpdate` ->
+`onTime` -> `activeCueIndex` (`web/src/pages/Review.tsx`).
+
+The player already has a cycling speed button (`RATES = [1, 1.25, 1.5, 2]`,
+`cycleRate` sets `a.playbackRate`). The requested spec is not fully met:
+
+- 0.75x is missing from the options.
+- A cycle button has no "selected option" state; reaching a specific speed
+  takes up to four presses.
+- `playbackRate` alone is reset by the browser if the media reloads; the
+  spec asks for the chosen speed to hold for the page's lifetime.
+
+This plan upgrades the control to an explicit selectable menu covering
+0.75x / 1x / 1.25x / 1.5x / 2x, applied immediately to the live element.
+
+## Governing records
+
+- ADR-001: this is a pure frontend change inside the browser app; no
+  backend route, schema, or storage change.
+- ADR-006: React + TypeScript + Tailwind + shadcn/ui on the web side; the
+  menu uses the existing `web/src/components/ui/select.tsx` (shadcn, added
+  via CLI previously) - no hand-rolled popup, no new dependencies. Type
+  gate `tsc --noEmit`; unit tests run under `vitest` in node environment.
+- BDR-002: zero added cost; local DOM API only.
+- PLAN-010 / PLAN-011 (implemented): introduced the Review player and the
+  cue-sync mechanism this plan touches; cue timestamps are media
+  `currentTime` positions, so sync is rate-independent by construction.
+
+## Scope
+
+In scope:
+
+1. `web/src/lib/playback-rates.ts` (new): the speed option list plus
+   small pure helpers, extracted so the option set is unit-testable under
+   the node test environment.
+2. `web/src/lib/playback-rates.test.ts` (new): vitest coverage for those
+   helpers.
+3. `web/src/components/audio-player.tsx`: replace the cycling ghost
+   `Button` with a compact `Select` bound to the same `rate` state; apply
+   the rate to the `<audio>` element immediately, including
+   `defaultPlaybackRate` so the choice survives a media reload.
+
+Out of scope:
+
+- Persistence beyond the page (no `localStorage`, no server field):
+  "stays selected while the user stays on the page" means component state
+  only.
+- Speed controls on the Live page, transcript PiP, or anywhere else.
+- Keyboard shortcuts for speed; `preservesPitch`/`mozPreservesPitch`
+  overrides (browser defaults stand).
+- Any change to cue parsing, marks, seek, or follow-scroll logic: sync is
+  derived from `currentTime`, which is already correct at every rate.
+
+## Contracts (literal)
+
+`web/src/lib/playback-rates.ts`:
+
+```ts
+export const PLAYBACK_RATES = [0.75, 1, 1.25, 1.5, 2] as const;
+export type PlaybackRate = (typeof PLAYBACK_RATES)[number];
+export const DEFAULT_PLAYBACK_RATE: PlaybackRate = 1;
+
+export function isPlaybackRate(v: number): v is PlaybackRate;
+export function rateLabel(rate: number): string; // `${rate}x`, e.g. "0.75x"
+```
+
+`SessionAudioPlayer` props are unchanged (no signature change; Review.tsx
+is untouched). The control is a controlled `Select`:
+
+```tsx
+<Select
+  value={String(rate)}
+  onValueChange={(v) => applyRate(Number(v))}
+>
+  <SelectTrigger
+    size="sm"
+    aria-label="Playback speed"
+    className="h-7 shrink-0 gap-1 rounded-md border-transparent px-1.5 font-mono text-xs tabular-nums hover:bg-accent hover:text-accent-foreground [&_svg]:size-3.5"
+  >
+    <SelectValue />
+  </SelectTrigger>
+  <SelectContent alignItemWithTrigger={false} className="min-w-20">
+    <SelectGroup>
+      {PLAYBACK_RATES.map((r) => (
+        <SelectItem
+          key={r}
+          value={String(r)}
+          className="font-mono text-xs tabular-nums"
+        >
+          {rateLabel(r)}
+        </SelectItem>
+      ))}
+    </SelectGroup>
+  </SelectContent>
+</Select>
+```
+
+Handler contract:
+
+```ts
+const applyRate = (next: number) => {
+  if (!isPlaybackRate(next)) return;
+  setRate(next);
+  const a = audioRef.current;
+  if (a) {
+    a.playbackRate = next;
+    a.defaultPlaybackRate = next;
+  }
+};
+```
+
+## Steps
+
+### Step 1 - `web/src/lib/playback-rates.ts` (new)
+
+- `PLAYBACK_RATES`, `PlaybackRate`, `DEFAULT_PLAYBACK_RATE`,
+  `isPlaybackRate`, `rateLabel` per the contract above.
+- `isPlaybackRate` is a `(PLAYBACK_RATES as readonly number[]).includes(v)`
+  membership check; `rateLabel` is a template literal, no rounding.
+
+### Step 2 - `web/src/components/audio-player.tsx`
+
+- Delete the local `const RATES = [1, 1.25, 1.5, 2]` and `cycleRate`.
+- Keep `const [rate, setRate] = useState(1)` but type it
+  `useState<PlaybackRate>(DEFAULT_PLAYBACK_RATE)` and import the helpers.
+- Add `applyRate` per the contract: sets state and writes both
+  `playbackRate` and `defaultPlaybackRate` on the element. Both writes are
+  immediate; the media never pauses or restarts. `defaultPlaybackRate`
+  pins the rate the browser falls back to on `load()`, so a reload of the
+  same `src` (e.g. after a transient network error) keeps the selection.
+- Replace the `<Button ...>{rate}x</Button>` block with the `Select`
+  contract above. Trigger styling mirrors the existing ghost `size-7`
+  buttons: borderless, `h-7`, mono tabular numerals, `hover:bg-accent`;
+  chevron shrinks to `size-3.5`. The trigger keeps
+  `aria-label="Playback speed"`.
+- The existing `rate` state already lives in `SessionAudioPlayer`, which
+  is mounted once per Review page view: the selection holds until the
+  user navigates away or reloads, matching "stays selected while the user
+  stays on the page".
+- Transcript sync needs no change: `onTimeUpdate` reports `currentTime`
+  in media seconds regardless of rate, and `activeCueIndex` maps that to
+  the same cue at any speed.
+
+### Step 3 - `web/src/lib/playback-rates.test.ts` (new)
+
+- `PLAYBACK_RATES` equals exactly `[0.75, 1, 1.25, 1.5, 2]` in order.
+- `isPlaybackRate` accepts each listed value and rejects e.g. `0.5`, `3`,
+  `NaN`.
+- `rateLabel` formats `0.75 -> "0.75x"`, `1 -> "1x"`, `2 -> "2x"`.
+
+## Test plan
+
+Automated (vitest, node environment):
+
+- New `playback-rates.test.ts` per Step 3. The player component itself
+  has no DOM test coverage precedent (vitest runs `environment: 'node'`
+  and no testing-library/jsdom is installed); extracting the option list
+  keeps the change covered without adding test infrastructure.
+
+Manual:
+
+- `npm run dev`, record a short session with audio on, open Review, press
+  Play, then switch speed mid-playback through each option including
+  0.75x: audio speed changes instantly, playback does not restart, the
+  trigger shows the new `Nx` label, and reopening the menu shows the same
+  item checked.
+- At 0.75x and 2x confirm the highlighted cue still tracks the audio and
+  follow-scroll stays aligned; click a cue timestamp and confirm seek
+  still lands on that segment.
+- Navigate to Sessions and back into the same Review: control resets to
+  1x (expected; persistence is page-scoped only).
+
+## Risks and notes
+
+- Assumption recorded (clarifications skipped per task instruction): the
+  spec's "the selected speed stays selected" is read as a selectable menu
+  with a persistent checked item, so the cycle button is replaced rather
+  than extended. If the reviewer prefers the minimal diff, the fallback
+  is keeping the cycle `Button` and setting `RATES = PLAYBACK_RATES` -
+  same lib module, same `applyRate` writes, one-line render change.
+- The transport row is compact; the pinned `border-transparent`/`h-7`
+  trigger classes keep the Select visually inline with the ghost
+  buttons. `alignItemWithTrigger={false}` drops the popover below the
+  trigger instead of overlaying it.
+- `audioRef.current` may be `null` before mount or after unmount; the
+  guard keeps `applyRate` safe, and the element is re-applied on the next
+  selection since `defaultPlaybackRate` is also written.
+- 0.75x is within `playbackRate` range on Chrome/Firefox/Safari for WAV;
+  pitch preservation is the browser default and is not overridden.
+- The `Select` popup renders in a portal at `z-50`, above the sticky
+  `z-10` player card; no stacking change needed.
+
+## Definition of Done
+
+- [ ] `npm test` green, including `playback-rates.test.ts`;
+      `npm run typecheck` clean.
+- [ ] All five speeds (0.75x, 1x, 1.25x, 1.5x, 2x) selectable in the
+      Review player; selection takes effect immediately with no playback
+      restart and the chosen item stays checked while on the page.
+- [ ] Both `audio.playbackRate` and `audio.defaultPlaybackRate` are
+      written on selection.
+- [ ] Manual check: cue highlight and follow-scroll remain correct at
+      0.75x and 2x; timestamp click-to-seek still works.
+- [ ] Plan status set to `implemented`; completion event logged.
-- 
2.50.0


